"female_cycle_desc_general" = "The menstrual cycle typically refers to the length of time from the first day of one period to the first day of the next. Normal menstrual cycles usually range from 21 to 35 days and last 2 to 7 days. However, cycle length varies from person to person and is affected by genetics, hormone levels, health, nutrition, and lifestyle.";
"female_cycle_desc_period" = "During menstruation, pay attention to personal hygiene and rest. Avoid strenuous exercise, cold water contact, and spicy foods. Maintain a good mood and eat iron-rich foods such as red meat and spinach.";
"female_cycle_desc_ovulation" = "During ovulation, the ovary releases a mature egg ready for fertilization. This is usually the best time for conception. Maintain good lifestyle habits, including proper diet, adequate sleep, moderate exercise, and avoid excessive stress.";
"female_cycle_desc_safe_period" = "Safe Period";
"female_cycle_record_time" = "Recorded to 'Fit-here' at";

